==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 20~80 seconds<sup>600f~2,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~66.67 seconds<sup>600f~2,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[One Horn]]s spawn, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Make sure to have all [[Treasure]]s from [[Empire of Cats]] before attempting this stage. The [[Blood Fruit]] and [[Sky Fruit]] from [[Into the Future]] are also beneficial, especially if you use a crowd controller-heavy list.

Spawn in [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] to hold back the lesser enemies that spawn in while you save up your money. Do not attack the enemy base for a while, as when you attack it, J.K. Bun Bun will be spawned. Once you have a max leveled [[Worker Cat]] and your wallet is as full as it can get, summon in every strong [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] or [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] cat that you have. Cats like [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Shaman Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] are very helpful here. As soon as J.K. Bun Bun appears, continue to deploy every cat you have along with Macho Cat and Wall Cat. This should hold him back and kill him off while cats like Bahamut Cat deal damage to him. Due to his high health, he may be a very difficult enemy to fight and the battle may last for a long time, but it is possible.

